    "body": "- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nWhen `evaluate_single == true`, it makes sense to me to clear the query after an item is activated.\r\n\r\nIf I'm reading it correctly, the only benefit to keeping the query string is to add more onto it, but `evaluate_single` has already ensured that the query string is at a leaf---adding more to the query string will never match any more or less than it does already.\r\n\r\nResetting the query string after activating a single item brings mini.nvim more in line with startify and alpha. Start screen items are logically discrete, and after activating one the need to backspace out the current query feels like a \"gotcha.\"",
    "closed_at": "2022-08-20T10:27:52Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nIf implemented as is, it feels a bit inconsistent with hitting `<CR>`, when item gets evaluated. In other words, if it is to be changed, it should be \"reset query when item is evaluated\". More so, it should be implemented to work when evaluation means \"close this buffer and open another\" (which is a most common use case). Quick test shows that it might cause hit-enter-prompt.\r\n\r\nInitial motivation for keeping a query string was to help when user mistypes. And also it seems to me a bit more intuitive to not automatically change query without user requesting so.\r\n\r\nAt the moment I am hesitant to add this. Main reason is that the design of item evaluation in Starter buffer is that it leads to closing current buffer, so it should not really matter. To mitigate the inconvenience, there is `<Esc>` that clears all query at once: one extra keystroke seems to not be *that* inconvenient. Also, if you use custom items, you should be able to add query reset in actions themselves.\r\n\r\nWould you mind sharing your use case in which not having this behavior causes you troubles?",
            "created_at": "2022-08-07T07:10:59Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/105#issuecomment-1207346139",
            "id": 1207346139,
