        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Hrmmn, I hadn't considered that, and that's a good point.\r\n\r\nI have multiple items in the Starter buffer that don't lead to closure. I have an options that run `PackerSync`, `PackerCompile`, and `GoUpdateBinaries`. I've been toying with items that open an `nvim-tree` window, reload my nvim config, etc. There are definitely creative things that could be good options for linkage from the Starter buffer. It's not unusual that I run `PackerSync` and then fire a `Telescope file_browser`, cancel it and browse a specfic dir, cancel it and open a blank buffer. Once an item is activated, my intent is always to run another; keeping the query string doesn't benefit me.\r\n\r\nThe behaviour that makes sense to me is for the query to be reset when an item is activated. If I activate an item and mini.starter is still open, I'm going to want to activate another item. Having the query retain the previous characters doesn't provide me any benefit.\r\n\r\nYou're absolutely right that `<Esc>` is a very minor inconvenience. My argument is that if it's not necessary, perhaps there's an opportunity to support that behaviour.\r\n\r\nPerhaps there's an opportunity for a `reset_query_after_action` option that globally clears the query after activation of any item? In startify and alpha modes, setting that option makes sense as it matches their behaviour.",
