        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Having the query retain the previous characters doesn't provide me any benefit.\r\n\r\nYes, I understand that. My original thinking was that it might benefit if latest character was a typo (not having to type whole query is a plus here) while having `<Esc>` allows dealing when this is not a typo. While resetting after evaluation doesn't provide an easy way in case of a typo.\r\n\r\n> Perhaps there's an opportunity for a reset_query_after_action option that globally clears the query after activation of any item?\r\n\r\nNot a fan of another option at the moment.\r\n\r\nI'll think about this a little more.",
