        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> Yes, I understand that. My original thinking was that it might benefit if latest character was a typo (not having to type whole query is a plus here) while having `<Esc>` allows dealing when this is not a typo. While resetting after evaluation doesn't provide an easy way in case of a typo.\r\n\r\nI can’t dispute that; it would certainly negate the benefits of typo correction.\r\n\r\nI will note that the startify/alpha paradigm commonly has single-character activators. In that modality, typo correction is not really a factor.",
